 "description": "The per-effect attribute bits, packed in SpellEffect.EffectAttributes: bit B is 1<<B. Names are wowdev.wiki's SpellEffectAttributes table (10.1.7); the bits the table leaves unnamed are listed by number so a row carrying one indexes a real entry. `server` records what the Epsilon core's spell code does with a bit; every other bit is client-side or unimplemented on that core and ships as a word to search by, never as a claim about behaviour. `handler` marks the bits that ship as flags on the effect kind, which is a data edit here plus the catalogue's own declaration of the word.",
 "source": [
  "https://wowdev.wiki/DB/SpellEffect",
